{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RoZgTrpXiq5YTJvo1dzJCf","type":"tool_result","content":"**2. Key Framework Elements Involved:**\r\n*   **Next.js App Router:** The new page will be created at `app/singapore-jobs/page.tsx`.\r\n*   **React Components:** The page and FAQ accordion will be implemented as functional React components.\r\n*   **JSON-LD Schema:** A script tag with `type=\"application/ld+json\"` for `FAQPage` must be generated and embedded in the page.\r\n\r\n**3. Recommended Implementation Approach:**\r\n1.  First, create the reusable `FaqAccordion.tsx` component to handle the display of question/answer pairs.\r\n2.  Next, implement the `generateFAQPage(title, faqItems)` function in `site/src/lib/structured-data.ts`.\r\n3.  Build the main page component `site/src/app/singapore-jobs/page.tsx`.\r\n4.  Inside this page, import and use the `FaqAccordion` and call `generateFAQPage` to create the JSON-LD structured data.\r\n5.  Add the \"Interview Stay Package\" CTA with a pre-filled WhatsApp inquiry link.\r\n6.  Finally, update `sitemap.ts` to ensure the new page is indexed.\r\n\r\n**4. Gotchas and Edge Cases:**\r\n*   **Diff Size Limit:** The story previously failed due to an `oversized_diff`. Implement changes in small, incremental steps to stay well under the 500-line limit.\r\n*   **Schema Validation:** The `FAQPage` JSON-LD must be syntactically correct and contain at least 8 question/answer entities to meet acceptance criteria.\r\n*   **CTA Functionality:** Ensure the WhatsApp link is correctly formatted and URL-encoded to pre-fill the message.\r\n*   **Build/Lint:** The final code must pass `npm run build` and `npm run lint` without errors.\r\n\r\n\r\n## Iteration 2 - Mon, Apr 14, 2026  5:45:00 AM\r\nCompleted: Create /singapore-jobs resource hub with FAQPage schema and job seeker CTAs (ID: US-262) — attempt 2\r\n\r\n### What was implemented\r\n- Created /singapore-jobs page with job overview, EP/S Pass/WP comparison table, FAQ accordion, booking CTA with WhatsApp link, and related blog post links\r\n- Created reusable FaqAccordion component in site/src/components/faq/FaqAccordion.tsx\r\n- Added FAQPage JSON-LD schema with 8 FAQ items covering work permits, salary, visa sponsorship, and job sectors\r\n- Updated sitemap.ts with /singapore-jobs URL\r\n\r\n### Patterns discovered\r\n- Visa-run page pattern: inline FAQPage schema as const, no separate structured-data.ts helper needed\r\n- Existing FAQ.tsx component is hostel-specific; created generic reusable FaqAccordion for topic-specific pages\r\n\r\n### Gotchas\r\n- Previous attempt produced 6609 lines — kept this attempt to 170 lines by using concise FAQ answers and following existing page patterns\r\n- No structured-data.ts file exists despite technical notes suggesting one; inline schema is the codebase pattern\r\n## Iteration 2 - Tue, Apr 14, 2026  5:40:05 AM\r\nCompleted: Create /singapore-jobs resource hub with FAQPage schema and job seeker CTAs (ID: US-262) in 7m\r\n\r\n## Iteration 1 - Tue, Apr 14, 2026  5:56:09 AM\r\nFAILED diff-guard: Add TikTok Pixel and Events API for Gen Z audience analytics (ID: US-171) — 7472 lines > 500 limit — attempt 1/3\r\n\r\n\r\n## Pre-analysis for US-171 (Gemini 2.5 Pro)\r\nThis user story is for a **Next.js/TypeScript** application, not Frappe/Python. The technical brief has been adjusted accordingly.\r\n\r\nHere is the technical brief for implementing the TikTok Pixel and Events API:\r\n\r\n### **Technical Brief: US-171 TikTok Integration**\r\n\r\n**1. Python/Frappe Files to Modify:**\r\nThis is a Next.js/TypeScript story. No Frappe/Python files are involved. The key files are within the `site/` directory.\r\n\r\n*   **`site/app/layout.tsx`**: To add the main TikTok Pixel script using `next/script`.\r\n*   **`site/app/api/tiktok-events/route.ts` (New File)**: To create the server-side Events API handler.\r\n*   **`site/lib/tiktok.ts` (New File)**: A helper module for client-side event tracking and sending data to our backend.\r\n*   Component Files: Files related to room/product pages (`ViewContent`), contact forms (`Contact`), and search functionality (`Search`) need to be modified to trigger tracking events.\r\n\r\n**2. Frappe DocTypes/Hooks:**\r\nNo Frappe DocTypes or hooks are involved. The implementation uses a Next.js API Route (`/api/tiktok-events`) and client-side event triggers.\r\n\r\n**3. Implementation Approach:**\r\n1.  **Layout (`layout.tsx`)**: Embed the TikTok Pixel base code using `<Script strategy='lazyOnload'>` to load it non-blockingly.\r\n2.  **API Route (`/api/tiktok-events/route.ts`)**:\r\n    *   Create a `POST` handler that receives event data (`event`, `event_id`, user data, etc.) from the client.\r\n    *   Retrieve the `TIKTOK_ACCESS_TOKEN` and `PIKTOK_PIXEL_CODE` from environment variables.\r\n    *   Use the Node.js `crypto` library to SHA-256 hash user data (email, phone).\r\n    *   Construct the event payload and `POST` it to the TikTok Events API (`https://business-api.tiktok.com/open_api/v1.3/event/track/`).\r\n3.  **Client-Side Helper (`lib/tiktok.ts`)**:\r\n    *   Create a function that generates a unique `event_id`.\r\n    *   This function will first trigger the browser-side event (`window.ttq.track(...)`).\r\n    *   Immediately after, it will `POST` the same event data (with the same `event_id`) to our `/api/tiktok-events` endpoint.\r\n4.  **Component Integration**: In the relevant components (e.g., on a room page `useEffect` or on a form `onSubmit`), call the client-side helper with the appropriate event name and properties.\r\n\r\n**4. Edge Cases & Gotchas:**\r\n*   **Secrets**: `TIKTOK_ACCESS_TOKEN` and `PIKTOK_PIXEL_CODE` must be stored securely in `.env.local` and not be exposed client-side.\r\n*   **Deduplication**: The `event_id` must be generated once per user action and used for *both* the client-side pixel call and the server-side API call. This is critical for achieving a high match rate.\r\n*   **Hashing**: All personally identifiable information (PII) like email and phone numbers must be hashed on the server-side in the API route before being sent to TikTok. Do not perform hashing on the client.\r\n*   **Timestamp**: Ensure the `timestamp` is in ISO 8601 format as required by the TikTok API.\r\n\r\n\r\n## Iteration 2 - Tue, Apr 14, 2026  (Attempt 2)\r\nCompleted: Add TikTok Pixel and Events API for Gen Z audience analytics (ID: US-171)\r\n\r\n### What was implemented\r\n- No new files needed — full implementation already committed in iter 22 (d7580bf)\r\n- Verified existing: site/src/app/api/tiktok-events/route.ts (Events API v1.3, SHA-256 hashing, event_id deduplication)\r\n- Verified existing: site/src/components/TikTokPixelProvider.tsx (lazyOnload Script, dual-signal, ViewContent/Contact/Search)\r\n- Verified: layout.tsx already imports TikTokPixelProvider via DynamicComponents\r\n\r\n### Patterns discovered\r\n- Previous attempt generated 7472-line diff by re-creating files that were already committed from iter 22\r\n- Always check git log for the specific files BEFORE writing new code to avoid re-implementing\r\n\r\n### Gotchas\r\n- The TikTok integration was already fully implemented; only prd.json needed updating\r\n- Build passes clean; all 5 code-verifiable acceptance criteria are satisfied\r\n## Iteration 1 - Tue, Apr 14, 2026  7:40:06 AM\nFAILED diff-guard: Apply CSS @starting-style for GPU-accelerated entry animations (ID: US-143) — 14829 lines > 500 limit — attempt 1/3\n[rerun: b2]","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"dbe161bb-03a2-4480-954a-17cda2fd68b8","uuid":"d23816e8-1def-4941-a729-ba4129cab828","timestamp":"2026-04-13T23:40:55.004Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"**2. Key Framework Elements Involved:**\r\n*   **Next.js App Router:** The new page will be created at `app/singapore-jobs/page.tsx`.\r\n*   **React Components:** The page and FAQ accordion will be implemented as functional React components.\r\n*   **JSON-LD Schema:** A script tag with `type=\"application/ld+json\"` for `FAQPage` must be generated and embedded in the page.\r\n\r\n**3. Recommended Implementation Approach:**\r\n1.  First, create the reusable `FaqAccordion.tsx` component to handle the display of question/answer pairs.\r\n2.  Next, implement the `generateFAQPage(title, faqItems)` function in `site/src/lib/structured-data.ts`.\r\n3.  Build the main page component `site/src/app/singapore-jobs/page.tsx`.\r\n4.  Inside this page, import and use the `FaqAccordion` and call `generateFAQPage` to create the JSON-LD structured data.\r\n5.  Add the \"Interview Stay Package\" CTA with a pre-filled WhatsApp inquiry link.\r\n6.  Finally, update `sitemap.ts` to ensure the new page is indexed.\r\n\r\n**4. Gotchas and Edge Cases:**\r\n*   **Diff Size Limit:** The story previously failed due to an `oversized_diff`. Implement changes in small, incremental steps to stay well under the 500-line limit.\r\n*   **Schema Validation:** The `FAQPage` JSON-LD must be syntactically correct and contain at least 8 question/answer entities to meet acceptance criteria.\r\n*   **CTA Functionality:** Ensure the WhatsApp link is correctly formatted and URL-encoded to pre-fill the message.\r\n*   **Build/Lint:** The final code must pass `npm run build` and `npm run lint` without errors.\r\n\r\n\r\n## Iteration 2 - Mon, Apr 14, 2026  5:45:00 AM\r\nCompleted: Create /singapore-jobs resource hub with FAQPage schema and job seeker CTAs (ID: US-262) — attempt 2\r\n\r\n### What was implemented\r\n- Created /singapore-jobs page with job overview, EP/S Pass/WP comparison table, FAQ accordion, booking CTA with WhatsApp link, and related blog post links\r\n- Created reusable FaqAccordion component in site/src/components/faq/FaqAccordion.tsx\r\n- Added FAQPage JSON-LD schema with 8 FAQ items covering work permits, salary, visa sponsorship, and job sectors\r\n- Updated sitemap.ts with /singapore-jobs URL\r\n\r\n### Patterns discovered\r\n- Visa-run