{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014KdfzYurBLb69v11x9s7AA","type":"tool_result","content":"commit b3c23545099d25b1565449556a34cce335bed4bb\nAuthor: wenjyue84 <wenjyue@gmail.com>\nDate:   Tue Apr 14 07:26:30 2026 +0800\n\n    feat: Apply CSS @starting-style for GPU-accelerated entry animations (US-143)\n    \n    - Add entry-fade-up class to CookieConsent banner with transition-behavior: allow-discrete for display:none animations\n    - Add entry-fade class to ExitIntentOverlay backdrop for smooth fade-in\n    - Add entry-zoom-in class to ExitIntentOverlay modal card for scale-in animation\n    - Add entry-zoom-in class to all three room card pricing cards (standard, premium, monthly)\n    - Add entry-fade class to SearchDialog backdrop for smooth fade-in\n    - Add entry-zoom-in class to SearchDialog dialog for scale-in animation\n    - Replace Tailwind animate-in utilities with custom @starting-style classes for GPU optimization\n    - All animations use only opacity + transform properties (GPU compositor thread)\n    - All animations respect prefers-reduced-motion per CSS rules in globals.css\n    \n    Story ID: US-143\n    Acceptance criteria met:\n    - [x] Room cards, modal overlays (SearchDialog, ExitIntentOverlay, CookieConsent), and cookie consent banner use @starting-style + transition instead of JavaScript\n    - [x] All entry animations paired with @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) override that disables motion\n    - [x] Animations use only transform and opacity properties for GPU compositor thread (no layout-triggering properties)\n    - [x] No new render-blocking resources introduced (animations already defined in globals.css)\n    - [x] CSS @starting-style syntax validated against MDN specification\n    \n    Co-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n site/src/components/CookieConsent.tsx     | 5 ++++-\n site/src/components/ExitIntentOverlay.tsx | 6 ++----\n site/src/components/RoomsTabs