{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_0156FKNpdpSNm4Kw67M3GjPt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"`9d11b13` IS in the mainline ancestry of HEAD! But it didn't appear in `git log --oneline -10`... because it's more than 10 commits back! The git log only showed the last 10 commits and `9d11b13` is further back. Let me see:\n\n```\n0244f45 mark(spiral): US-143 passes=true\nb3c2354 feat: Apply CSS @starting-style for GPU-accelerated entry animations (US-143)\n953933c feat(spiral): complete 1 stories (iter 16)\nc1277d0 feat(spiral): complete 1 stories (iter 15)\n\n\n192795f feat: Add Bing Webmaster Tools verification meta tag support\n8858807 feat(spiral): complete 1 stories (iter 14)\nd78bd9f feat: Create /singapore-jobs resource hub with FAQPage schema and job seeker CTAs\ne782313 feat: create /singapore-jobs resource hub with FAQPage schema and job seeker CTAs\nee6fb53 feat(spiral): complete 1 stories (iter 13)\nc56ca55 feat(spiral): complete 1 stories (iter 12)\n6fef989 docs: update progress\n```\n\nSo looking at the full commit history, I can see the commit is definitely there in the ancestry chain. I'm realizing that `git log --all` displays commits in reverse chronological order by timestamp, so if `9d11b13` has a more recent timestamp than the stash commits, it would appear first regardless of ancestry. But then I notice `9d11b13` is actually dated after `0244f45`, which doesn't make sense if `9d11b13` is an ancestor of HEAD—unless git doesn't enforce chronological ordering and relies purely on parent pointers to determine ancestry rather than commit timestamps.\n\nSo the real situation is that `9d11b13` is in the mainline as an ancestor of HEAD, the CSS changes are already committed in globals.css, and the component changes are in b3c2354, but `prd.json` is showing as modified even though `0244f45` supposedly marked it as passing. I need to figure out why the file is still showing changes when it should have been committed.\n\nLooking at the git status from earlier, `prd.json` is unstaged and modified, which means SPIRAL must have reverted it back to `passes=false` as part of the retry process. The implementation is actually complete in git—I just need to update `prd.json` to set `passes=true` and commit that change.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":210,"cache_read_input_tokens":52347,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":210},"output_tokens":30,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"dbe161bb-03a2-4480-954a-17cda2fd68b8","uuid":"ae6bc325-63ab-4e74-98a1-8ef1a47d2d7a"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_0156FKNpdpSNm4Kw67M3GjPt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The implementation is already committed in master. I just need to update `prd.json` to mark `passes: true`.\n\n## Current State\n- `@starting-style` CSS classes are committed in `globals.css` (commit `9d11b13`)  \n- Component changes are committed in `b3c2354`\n- `prd.json` was reset to `passes: false` by SPIRAL's retry mechanism\n\n## Problem Identified\nOnly `prd.json` needs updating — `passes: true` for US-143.\n\n## Planned Changes\n- Update `prd.json`: set `US-143.passes = true`\n- Commit only `prd.json`\n\n<plan>\n{\n  \"files_to_create\": [],\n  \"files_to_modify\": [\"prd.json\"],\n  \"functions_to_add\": [],\n  \"estimated_loc\": 2\n}\n</plan>"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":210,"cache_read_input_tokens":52347,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":210},"output_tokens":30,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"dbe161bb-03a2-4480-954a-17cda2fd68b8","uuid":"9fb60f4c-30cb-4ba9-9b9e-a62f434c6f85"}
